{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793051794,"nonce":"dPtvT7OUzY3gvWsVk4tKVl+EQAk=","title":"Preserve map literals across macro Expr ADT reconstruction","message":"A map expression is encoded as EArrayDecl containing OpArrow expressions, as in Haxe's macro API. Decoding currently reconstructs every EArrayDecl as an ordinary array, so changing an expression's position loses Map semantics. This can also prevent macro typing probes from checking heterogeneous map keys or values.\n\nReproducer: MacroMapRoundTrip.hx in haxe-conformance/regressions creates a map through a macro that changes e.pos, then calls get on its entries. The Expr ADT unit test must retain ExprKind::Map after def_of/try_expr_of. Stock Haxe accepts the executable fixture. Audit the related corpus map-probe cases, including Issue3935, without changing the corpus assertions.","files":null}]}